# Design-system conformance

When the user shares a Figma URL, screen, or asks to implement/build a design,
map instances 1:1 to the catalog components, importing each from the package
index (`import { Button, TextField } from '@ds/ui'`). Do not invent styles,
hex colors, or extra RN `style` props.

Catalog (Figma Components page): Text, Button, Card, Section, Container, Icon, List, Sheet, Loading, Hud, Breadcrumbs, Header, TextField, Select, DateTimePicker, Pin, Tckn, Form, ProgressBar, Dots, BarGraph, LineGraph, SliderCarousel. Inputs, stepper, and graphs all resolve from `@ds/ui`. Form bindings live in `@ds/controller` (`Form`, `Form.TextField`, …). Web header is Breadcrumbs (`Header.web.tsx`).

Repeating rows are a list, not a stack of instances: render them with
`List` from `@ds/ui` (virtualized) instead of mapping the array into a column.
List draws no chrome of its own, so this does not change the design.

Device chrome (status bar, home indicator) is allowed on phone frames. It is not a product component.

Layout frames / groups / slots are fine around instances. Raw TEXT, RECTANGLE, VECTOR, or instances of any other component mean the design is off-catalog: say so and ask before implementing.

Never draw a custom control to "match" a non-DS frame. Never silently restyle a DS component to approximate a one-off design.
